Subject: [PATCH 10/22] feat(intros): the bridge most likely to say yes comes
 first; both sides pre-cleared (1697, A14 part 1)

D679/D680. The warm path named its bridges in order of reach, so a request
could start towards a bridge who would never take it, a wait for nothing.

- find_warm_path, given the open goal's words, now orders paths within the
  same number of hops. The first bridge's pre-match (A11, from his own data)
  comes first, then his answer rate in the goal's field (A8), then the rarer
  shared contact (fewer phonebooks hold him) before the famous one. Nothing
  new is shown: only the order moves (D680: no private fact as a reason).
  With no goal, or on any failed read, the order is as before.
- Migration 224: every introduction request records the bridge's and the
  receiver's pre-match at the same moment, from the goal it was raised for.
  It is for the admin only, written after the send, and never tells the
  receiver anything. He still hears only after the bridge's yes (D438).

Not in this part: when every bridge and the receiver are not_his_field, no
request should be made and the plan should say the route looks closed. That
needs a new model-facing line (D44), so it waits for Misho's yes.

DONE WHEN (this part): on seats where A reaches C through B1 (fits, answers)
and B2 (nothing known), find_warm_path lists B1's path first; the request's
row shows bridge_prematch and receiver_prematch written together; C receives
nothing until B1 taps yes.

